### 4.4 Results

In 3.36M recorded, unbiased events a \({}^{3}\overline{\mathrm{He}}\) raw yield of 193 was found. Therefore, with a \(Z=-2\) trigger efficiency of 80%, an absolute enhancement of 32 \({}^{3}\overline{\mathrm{He}}\) particles is expected in 0.7M events scanned by L3. The offline reconstructed yield of 28 candidates from the 867 triggered events on tape is in rather good agreement with this expectation. Figure 4.10 shows the raw yield as a function of transverse momentum from the offline reconstruction of the unbiased and the triggered events. The enhancement in the \(dE/dx\) spectrum is displayed in Figure 4.11.

Finally, a comparison of the physics analysis results, with and without the triggered events included in the data sample, allows to test the capabilities of the Level-3 trigger system to improve physics observables. The details of

